  "aiContextParagraph": "The controversy follows a match between PSS Sleman and Arema FC in the BRI Super League, which resulted in a 0-3 defeat for PSS Sleman. Following the loss, supporters engaged in disruptive behavior, including damaging stadium property such as the goal nets. In response, PSSI chairman Erick Thohir confirmed that the governing body is in discussions with FIFA regarding the incident. PSSI is coordinating with Indonesian police to investigate the disturbances, while the I.League has publicly advocated for strict disciplinary measures to be imposed by the PSSI Disciplinary Committee. Suggestions have been made to implement temporary bans for supporters attending stadium events. PSS Sleman, which had been focusing on physical and defensive training during the league break, has since issued a formal response regarding the conduct of its fan base during the match.",
